<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Grodziec Castle</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Grodziec Castle stands on a basalt hill in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-silesia">Lower Silesia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, near Złotoryja. A stronghold there is first recorded in the 12th century; the castle was rebuilt in stone by the dukes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legnica">Legnica</a> in the 15th century and wrecked in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War. It was reconstructed in historicist style in the early 20th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/grodziec-castle.jpg" alt="Grodziec Castle" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Edward Knapczyk · CC BY-SA 3.0 pl · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mury_zamkowe_(07.2011).JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
